     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That's about twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity. It may be a typo, such as 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,700 mg total per day.\n\n2. **You're not a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a licensed clinician, who can confirm the indication, dose, and patient details. Pharmacy would normally verify the order too.\n\nPlease have the prescribing clinician confirm the intended dose. I can enter the order once a clinician gives me a corrected dose, or if they confirm the dose is deliberate and add a note saying so."
      }
     ],
