     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum labeled dose, and I can't verify any clinical reason for it.\n- **The confirmation has to come from the prescriber.** You've told me you're a financial analyst, not a clinician. Your confirmation can't replace a prescriber's review of the dose.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating physician or other licensed prescriber to review the intended dose.\n- If the dose is a typo, they can give me the corrected one. For example, 850 mg three times daily is 2,550 mg/day.\n- If they really want the higher dose, they can enter it themselves or tell me directly. Pharmacy would likely want to verify it as well.\n\nI'm glad to enter the order once a prescriber gives me a dose within the labeled range, or confirms a different dose themselves."
      }
     ],
